{
  "duration": 197.85000610351562,
  "language": "english",
  "text": "Thanks so much for the question. This question is around live markets. The first thing I would say is go check out our interview on our YouTube with Ed Miller. Ed Miller runs and created the company Huddle with Matthew Davidow who are the providers for all of the live lines for the major books like Vandal and DraftKings. That being said, I'll kind of summarize what it is he's taught us and we've communicated with him and as well as what he's written about in his books, Logic of Sports Betting and Interception. But remember because the main size and totals undergo a market dynamic, those closing lines are quite informed. And then the live markets however are not undergoing any market making process. All this is is a model like Huddles that is using the closing line and some other information in from the game to originate a number. You know Ed Miller's opinion on this I don't want to I don't want to speak for him but the things that you know I've taken away from the conversations we've had are that you know if you're if you're talking first quarter you know differences between the main market and what the live line is it's probably pretty sharp still because that it's informed still by what the closing line is and that's still very predictive and so when you're when you're early on in the game not much has really changed even if there is one score you know this way or that way. He thinks that the later in the game you get the more edge there is. That being said there are definitely edges in live markets no doubt about it at all because again you're not actually being a market now you're just needing to be one person's model and if there are flaws with that model with how they're deriving things like maybe they just use an you know averages for you know every team you know they use league averages that's probably wrong so they're definitely edges there. I would read Interception and I would go check out some interviews with Ed Miller like I said there's one on our YouTube that we did with him. The other thing I would caution is it's perceived you know your perceived edge I see what you're saying you think that there's a lot of value and I'm not saying that there's that you don't actually have that but what I would not I would challenge you to is can you actually track this so you start betting you know bet small or even log it and don't actually bet real money or bet small can you actually see that you have a positive ROI. There are some benefits about betting in a live market this is a market that the books want you to be betting into and there's really no such thing as closing line value in this market so it's really hard to get limited unless you're doing arbitrage betting and kind of taking advantage of errors but if you're just truly better than the book at modeling or thinking through some of these spots my understanding is it's actually a lot harder to get limited because again there isn't the same metrics like closing line value to be able to calculate so that's where I would start that's where I would get a lot more deeper information and those are kind of my opinions on it I hope it helps let us know if you have any other questions",
